    {
      "line_range": "L57-60",
      "text": "The `terraform.state.S3Reference` class exists in the `@pulumi/terraform` package and accepts `bucket` and `key` arguments to reference Terraform state stored in S3.",
      "type": "api-surface",
      "source_hint": "@pulumi/terraform",
      "confidence": "high",
      "file": "content/docs/iac/get-started/terraform/next-steps.md",
      "found_by": [
        "llm-atomic"
      ]
    },
    {
      "line_range": "L53-54",
      "text": "`new pulumi.StackReference(\"core-infra\")` with `getOutput(\"vpcId\")` retrieves an output from another Pulumi stack.",
      "type": "api-surface",
      "source_hint": "Pulumi",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "file": "content/docs/iac/get-started/terraform/next-steps.md",
      "found_by": [
        "llm-atomic"
      ]
    },
    {
      "line_range": "L80-81",
      "text": "`S3Reference` objects expose a `getOutput` method returning Terraform state outputs (e.g. `private_subnet_ids`).",
      "type": "api-surface",
      "source_hint": "@pulumi/terraform",
      "confidence": "high",
      "file": "content/docs/iac/get-started/terraform/next-steps.md",
      "found_by": [
        "llm-atomic"
      ]
    },
    {
      "line_range": "L84-92",
      "text": "The `aws.ecs.Cluster` resource accepts a `configuration.executeCommandConfiguration` argument with `kmsKeyId` and `logging` properties, where `logging: \"DEFAULT\"` is a valid value.",
      "type": "api-surface",
      "source_hint": "pulumi/pulumi-aws",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "file": "content/docs/iac/get-started/terraform/next-steps.md",
      "found_by": [
        "llm-atomic"
      ]
    },
    {
      "line_range": "L101",
      "text": "`pulumi import` can be used to bring Terraform-managed resources under Pulumi management.",
      "type": "behavior",
      "confidence": "high",
      "file": "content/docs/iac/get-started/terraform/next-steps.md",
      "found_by": [
        "llm-atomic"
      ]
    },
    {
      "line_range": "L103",
      "text": "State ownership can be transferred from Terraform to Pulumi gradually, resource-by-resource.",
      "type": "feature",
      "confidence": "low",
      "file": "content/docs/iac/get-started/terraform/next-steps.md",
      "found_by": [
        "llm-atomic"
      ]
    },
    {
      "line_range": "L110-112",
      "text": "`pulumi import` accepts the syntax `pulumi import <type> <name> <id>`, e.g. `pulumi import aws:ec2/vpc:Vpc main-vpc vpc-12345`, and the type tokens `aws:ec2/vpc:Vpc`, `aws:ec2/subnet:Subnet`, and `aws:ecs/cluster:Cluster` are valid.",
      "type": "api-surface",
      "source_hint": "pulumi/pulumi-aws",
      "confidence": "high",
      "file": "content/docs/iac/get-started/terraform/next-steps.md",
      "found_by": [
        "llm-atomic"
      ]
    },
    {
      "line_range": "L122-127",
      "text": "The `getOutput(\"resources\")` method on `terraform.state.S3Reference` returns a value that can be awaited and filtered as an array of resources with `type` and `name` fields.",
      "type": "api-surface",
      "source_hint": "@pulumi/terraform",
      "confidence": "low",
      "file": "content/docs/iac/get-started/terraform/next-steps.md",
      "found_by": [
        "llm-atomic"
      ]
    },
    {
      "line_range": "L147",
      "text": "Pulumi policies (CrossGuard/Policy as Code) can enforce infrastructure policies that work across both Terraform and Pulumi resources.",
